  "question": {
    "text": "A long string is stretched by $2 \\mathrm{~cm}$ and the potential energy is $\\mathrm{V}$. If the spring is stretched by $10 \\mathrm{~cm}$, its potential energy will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{V} / 25$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{V} / 5$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5 \\mathrm{~V}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$25 \\mathrm{~V}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad V=\\frac{1}{2} k(x)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2} k(2)^{2}$ or $k=\\frac{2 V}{4}=\\frac{V}{2}$\n$$\n\\mathrm{V}^{\\prime}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{k}(10)^{2}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{2}\\right)(10)^{2}=25 \\mathrm{~V}\n$$"
  }
}